---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="API and MCP for AIs · OpenCyber Academy" description="Connect agents to OpenCyber Academy's public books with MCP, REST and Markdown.">
  <section class="ai-hero"><div class="shell"><div class="eyebrow">LIBRARY FOR AIs</div><h1>Verifiable knowledge,<br /><span class="gold-text">accessible by protocol.</span></h1><p>OpenCyber Academy offers the same books to human readers and agents. Discover courses, consult the index and read published chapters. Every result identifies its public source.</p><div class="hero-links"><a class="button gold" href="/levels/">Explore lessons ↗</a><a class="button secondary" href="/api/docs">Open OpenAPI ↗</a></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell ai-grid"><div class="card ai-card"><span class="eyebrow">01 · MCP</span><h2>Connect an agent</h2><p>Use the public HTTP endpoint in an MCP client that accepts remote servers. Reading books requires no account or key.</p><div class="endpoint"><code>https://opencyber.academy/mcp</code><button id="copy-mcp" type="button" aria-label="Copy MCP URL">Copy</button></div><p class="muted tiny">Tools include <code>get_editorial_policy</code>, <code>list_courses</code>, <code>list_lessons</code>, <code>read_lesson</code> and <code>search_course</code>. Resources include the catalog, editorial policy and chapters.</p></div><div class="card ai-card"><span class="eyebrow">02 · REST API</span><h2>Integrate without an SDK</h2><p>The catalog and each lesson are available as JSON. Complete manuscripts are available as Markdown from the public editorial source.</p><pre><code>GET /api/catalog
GET /api/courses/&#123;level&#125;/&#123;area&#125;/&#123;language&#125;
GET /api/lessons/&#123;level&#125;/&#123;area&#125;/&#123;language&#125;/&#123;chapter&#125;
GET /api/books/&#123;level&#125;/&#123;area&#125;/&#123;language&#125;
GET /api/search/&#123;level&#125;/&#123;area&#125;/&#123;language&#125;?q=...</code></pre><a class="text-link" href="/api/openapi.json">OpenAPI specification →</a></div></div></section>
  <section class="section steps"><div class="shell"><div class="eyebrow">FROM COURSE TO CHAPTER</div><h2>Three steps to consult the library.</h2><div class="step-grid"><div class="card step"><span>1</span><h3>Discover</h3><p>List the 207 courses and choose a language, subject and level. The catalog gives the structure; the book is checked again when a lesson opens.</p></div><div class="card step"><span>2</span><h3>Locate</h3><p>Browse subjects in study order. Each is marked as a published lesson or a planned chapter.</p></div><div class="card step"><span>3</span><h3>Read and cite</h3><p>Read the lesson and worked answers. Use its public source URL when citing the original text.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="eyebrow">PRIVATE STUDENT MCP</div><h2>Connect your AI to your own study record.</h2><p class="muted">Sign in to your student area and create a personal key in “Connect your AI”. Use an MCP client that supports private HTTP headers:</p><pre><code>URL: https://opencyber.academy/mcp
Authorization: Bearer &lt;your-personal-key&gt;</code></pre><p class="muted">The key appears once. Keep it in the client's private credential field, never in a prompt or a URL. It expires after 180 days and can be revoked from your account. Authenticated study actions count toward your own dashboard and are labeled as AI activity.</p><p class="muted">Student tools can record lesson visits, completion, exercise answers, analyses and timed chapter tests, then read progress, saved analyses and results. Public books remain readable without signing in.</p><a class="button gold" href="/account/#connect-ai">Connect your AI →</a></div></section>
  <section class="section source-note"><div class="shell"><h2>One source, open access.</h2><p>The API and each permanent HTML lesson page read manuscripts from the public <code>main</code> branch. Each authored unit also has a permanent <code>.md</code> response derived from that same book. Editing a numbered lesson updates its page, Markdown response, course directory and per-course sitemap without rebuilding the site. A new book edition or course still needs a local deployment for catalog discovery. A public lesson does not mean its entire book passed editorial review.</p><p>The editorial production order is English, then Portuguese, then Spanish. Work on the other six languages begins after all three collections meet the full completion and review gate. Read the current rule through the MCP <code>get_editorial_policy</code> tool or <code>open-cyber-academy://editorial-policy</code> resource.</p><p>For a reader-facing citation, use a permanent lesson URL such as <a href="/courses/rapid-1-month/incident-response-resilience/lessons/en/1/">rapid incident response, lesson 1</a>. For machine-readable text and hashes, use the public API or MCP.</p><div class="inline-links"><a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt ↗</a><a href="/sitemap.xml">Sitemap ↗</a><a href="/read/?path=AI_GUIDE.md">Guide for agents ↗</a><a href="/read/?path=RIGHTS.md">Usage rights ↗</a></div></div></section>
  <script>
    document.getElementById('copy-mcp')?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText('https://opencyber.academy/mcp');
      const button = document.getElementById('copy-mcp')!; button.textContent = 'Copied';
      setTimeout(() => { button.textContent = 'Copy'; }, 1800);
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .ai-hero { padding: 105px 0 90px; background: linear-gradient(110deg, var(--bg-2), var(--bg)); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }.ai-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.6rem,5vw,5rem); }.ai-hero p { max-width: 760px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.12rem; }.hero-links { display: flex; gap: 12px; margin-top: 27px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .ai-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2,1fr); gap: 22px; }.ai-card { padding: 32px; }.ai-card h2 { font-size: 1.7rem; margin: 13px 0; }.ai-card p { color: var(--muted); }.endpoint { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 14px; background: var(--bg-2); border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 13px; border-radius: 4px; overflow: auto; }.endpoint code { white-space: nowrap; color: var(--gold); }.endpoint button { background: var(--royal); color: white; border: 0; border-radius: 4px; padding: 7px 11px; }.tiny { font-size: .78rem; margin-top: 22px; }.ai-card pre { background: var(--bg-2); color: var(--text); border-radius: 4px; padding: 18px; overflow-x: auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: .83rem; }.text-link,.inline-links a { color: var(--gold); font-weight: 600; }
  .steps { background: var(--bg-2); }.step-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3,1fr); gap: 18px; margin-top: 26px; }.step { padding: 25px; box-shadow: none; }.step span { color: var(--gold); font: 600 1.5rem 'Titillium Web',sans-serif; }.step h3 { font-size: 1.15rem; }.step p { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; margin-bottom: 0; }.source-note { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }.source-note p { color: var(--muted); max-width: 810px; }.source-note p a { color: var(--gold); text-decoration: underline; }.inline-links { display: flex; gap: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 26px; }
  @media(max-width:800px){.ai-grid,.step-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.ai-hero{padding:70px 0}.ai-card{padding:24px}}
</style>
